From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 00:50:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] tools: BD-Live in the BD-J server: TCP over IPv4 only,
 the filter of addresses checked

With HADES_BDJ_NETWORK=internet (hades-bdj-net@.service), the server's seccomp filter allows
sockets of AF_UNIX and TCP over IPv4 only: no IPv6, no UDP or other socket type, no protocol but
TCP; and nothing listens or accepts.

The addresses are limited by the unit (IPAddressDeny=, a BPF filter of the kernel on the
instance's cgroup). systemd starts a unit without it, with a warning, where the kernel cannot do
it, so before the filter takes UDP away the server sends a datagram to loopback and to a
documentation address and ends unless the kernel refuses both (EPERM). Measured on the build host:
a TCP connection to a refused address is not refused at once (its SYN is dropped and connect()
waits), a datagram is; without the filter it goes. It also reads the subnets of this system's
interfaces while netlink is there, for the Java check (HADES_BDJ_BDLIVE_LOCAL).
---
 src/tools/hades_bdj_sandbox.c     |  26 ++--
 src/tools/hades_bdj_sandbox_net.c | 201 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/tools/hades_bdj_sandbox_net.h |  40 ++++++
 src/tools/meson.build             |   2 +-
 4 files changed, 256 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 src/tools/hades_bdj_sandbox_net.c
 create mode 100644 src/tools/hades_bdj_sandbox_net.h

